    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124-a3">

                <pb facs="0252" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg158"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    153.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Amunátegui to Mr. Roberts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-06"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 6,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The widow of the former envoy extraordinary
                    and minister plenipotentiary of the United States of America in Chili, General
                    Judson Kilpatrick, having determined to remove to their native land the remains
                    of her late husband, services will be held on the occasion in the cathedral
                    church on next Friday, the 9th instant, at 10 o’clock in the forenoon.</p>
                <p>Afterwards the remains of General Kilpatrick will be conducted to the railroad
                    station with the usual honors.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to invite the legation under your worthy charge in order that
                    you and the persons composing it may please, if so disposed, to be present at
                    said services.</p>
                <p>Renewing, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Miguel Luis
                    Amunátegui.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
